Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:17:51 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] feat(nfc): fill a tag's filament from SpoolmanDB for
 every brand

SpoolmanDB was only used for Bambu tags. A tag written with a phone app carries brand, material and colour, and often the app's generic temperatures. An unknown tag of any brand is now looked up in Spoolman's copy of SpoolmanDB (/v1/external/filament): same manufacturer and material, closest colour within an RGB distance of 60, the tag's material detail breaking ties. A match gives the manufacturer's name, temperatures (they win over the tag's), density and spool weight, and its SpoolmanDB id as external_id, so a filament already imported from SpoolmanDB in Spoolman is reused. Without a match, or with an older Spoolman, the tag data is used as before.
